      "body": "- `enter_late_layer_tail` on the CUDA and HIP DeepSeek V4 backends takes an optional `metadata` argument; without it the backend uses `tail_forward_metadata` as before.\n- The prefill-graph break passes the exact-row tail metadata it builds to `enter_late_layer_tail`, instead of swapping it into `backend.tail_forward_metadata` and restoring the held value in a `finally`. The break no longer writes that backend field.\n- No behavior change, on the normal and the exception path: the backend state after the call and the value returned are the same. The model's own tail path does not pass `metadata` and is unchanged.\n- First step toward giving the late-layer tail a single owner. The earlier content of this PR (shared row selection, graph gate and DP rows) is dropped here and comes back in later PRs.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40425814666](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40425814666)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40425814626](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40425814626)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #40425814648](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40425814648)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
